35,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"The logs show eleven misrouted deliveries, all from duplicate addresses. We also lose an hour daily copying records.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, that daily hour is a leak. My data is worse: two people write every log by hand, and our devs are locked until Q3.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, your staffing crisis is real, but my data is worse. Half the plants lose coverage afternoons, and device approval took six weeks. We cannot build on sand.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, access is critical, but my data shows the capital line is frozen. Only the recurring software allowance remains. We must fund within that narrow, recurring pocket.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Ryuji, that’s a huge constraint! My data shows broad tools get dropped, but narrow ones survive. We must pick a tool for one specific trade, not everyone.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Kenji, that matches my logs. The duplicate addresses are a narrow, specific failure. A tool for one trade could fix that daily leak.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, exactly. A narrow tool fixes the leak without demanding my two exhausted coordinators. We need something that runs itself, not another manual chore.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, a self-running tool is useless if it can’t reach the site. My data proves half the plants are offline afternoons. We need a candidate that works offline or has a local cache.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, offline capability is essential. But my data shows per-head licences climb with every department. We must avoid broad, multi-department tools to stay within the recurring allowance.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Ryuji, you’re right! Broad tools cost too much. My data proves narrow tools survive. We need a specific, affordable fix that doesn’t need everyone’s attention.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Shunichi, I agree. The offline constraint is vital. My data shows the copying loss is local. A tool that works without constant connection would finally stop that daily hour.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, offline is non-negotiable. My coordinators are drowning in manual logs. We need a tool that runs locally, so they don’t have to chase connectivity or copy data by hand.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, precisely. If the signal dies, the tool must still function. I will verify if the vendor’s local cache handles the six-week approval lag.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, the local cache is vital, but the cost structure is the final gate. Per-head pricing makes broad tools unaffordable. We need a fixed-fee, narrow solution.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Ryuji, fixed-fee is perfect! My data shows narrow tools survive because they’re simple. A fixed-fee, offline tool for one trade is the only path that works for us all.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"@Kenji, I agree. A fixed-fee, offline tool for one trade fits our reality. It stops the daily copying without breaking the budget.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,May,,"@Kenji, I’m with you. A fixed-fee tool means no new heads to manage. My coordinators can finally breathe. Let’s pick the one that runs itself.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Kenji, I agree. A fixed-fee, offline tool respects the six-week approval lag. It’s the only option that doesn’t rely on external access we don’t control.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Kenji, I concur. Fixed-fee avoids the per-head trap. It fits the frozen capital line. We must choose the narrow, offline solution that respects our financial reality.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Ryuji, I’m so happy we all agree! A fixed-fee, offline tool for one trade is the clear winner. It respects our budget and history. I vote for it!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
